  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting MS on resilient water management through citizen and open sciences</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity aims to transform water management paradigms, aligning with global climate and development goals. Advocating for resilience, it integrates citizen science, open science to address climate resilient water management using CRIDA. Diverging from traditional top-down approaches, the initiative endorses new methods that assess uncertainties and engage stakeholders from the outset. Applying CRIDA comprehensively to pilot sites, the project analyzes climate-sensitive indicators, offering adaptation pathways. Leveraging citizen science, it promotes e-learning, tools development, participatory monitoring, and inclusive decision-making. The initiative also further developed open science in hydrology, encouraging collaboration, capacity building, and open-source solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
